# 2. MVC Architecture Overview

## Model

Represents the MongoDB schemas and database collections.

Examples:

* Product
* Category
* Brand
* User
* Cart
* Wishlist
* Order

## View

ReactJS frontend responsible for rendering the user interface.

Examples:

* Home Page
* Product Listing
* Product Details
* Cart Page
* Wishlist Page
* Checkout Page
* User Dashboard
* Admin Dashboard

## Controller

Receives HTTP requests and sends responses.

Responsibilities:

* Validate requests
* Call Service layer
* Return API responses

## Service

Contains all business logic.

Examples:

* Add product to cart
* Remove from wishlist
* Calculate cart total
* Process checkout
* Validate stock

## Repository

Responsible for all database operations.

Responsibilities:

* Create
* Read
* Update
* Delete (CRUD)

---

## Request Flow

```text
React Frontend
      │
      ▼
REST API
      │
      ▼
Controller
      │
      ▼
Service
      │
      ▼
Repository
      │
      ▼
MongoDB
```

