# 3. Add to Cart Functionality

The Add to Cart feature allows customers to save products for purchase while maintaining selected product variants such as size, color, quantity, and price.

## Frontend (ReactJS)

### Features

* Add product from Product Listing page
* Add product from Product Details page
* Select size and color before adding
* Increase or decrease quantity
* Remove product from cart
* Display cart item count in the header
* Store cart in Redux Context or Local Storage for guest users
* Synchronize cart with the backend after user login

## Backend

### Cart APIs

* Add Product to Cart
* Get User Cart
* Update Cart Quantity
* Remove Cart Item
* Clear Cart

## Cart Collection Example

```javascript
{
    userId,
    items: [
        {
            productId,
            variantId,
            quantity,
            price
        }
    ]
}
```

## Flow

```text
Product Page
      │
Click Add to Cart
      │
      ▼
React API Call
      │
      ▼
Cart Controller
      │
      ▼
Cart Service
      │
      ▼
Cart Repository
      │
      ▼
MongoDB
```

---

# 4. Add to Wishlist Functionality

Wishlist allows customers to save products for future purchase without adding them to the shopping cart.

## Frontend (ReactJS)

### Features

* Add to Wishlist
* Remove from Wishlist
* Heart icon toggle
* Wishlist page
* Display wishlist count in header
* Move item from Wishlist to Cart

## Backend

### Wishlist APIs

* Add Product to Wishlist
* Get Wishlist
* Remove Product from Wishlist
* Clear Wishlist

## Wishlist Collection Example

```javascript
{
    userId,
    products: [
        productId
    ]
}
```

## Flow

```text
Product Page
      │
Click Wishlist Button
      │
      ▼
React API Call
      │
      ▼
Wishlist Controller
      │
      ▼
Wishlist Service
      │
      ▼
Wishlist Repository
      │
      ▼
MongoDB
```

---

# 5. Cart & Wishlist Integration

### Guest User

* Cart data stored in Local Storage
* Wishlist stored in Local Storage

### Logged-in User

* Cart stored in MongoDB
* Wishlist stored in MongoDB
* Local Storage data synchronized after login

